     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I am using facet to plot box plots.  the facets are separated by 2 states, however, one of the x axis categories does not apply for one of the states. Since there is no data for that category.  I do not want to show it at all in the plot.  Is there a way to limit that?  here is the code and data.  Basically I don&#39;t want category &quot;B&quot; to be show for state NY.<br>\r\n<br>Thanks,<br><br><br><br></div><u><b>CODE</b></u><br>ggplot(table, aes(x=Category, y=Value, fill=Category)) + geom_boxplot()+ facet_grid(.~ State)<br><div><br><br><u><b>DATA</b></u><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:195pt\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"195\">\r\n\r\n <colgroup><col style=\"width:65pt\" span=\"3\" width=\"65\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt;width:65pt\" height=\"15\" width=\"65\">State</td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:65pt\" width=\"65\">Value</td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:65pt\" width=\"65\">Category</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">CA</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">323</td>\r\n  <td>A</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">CA</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">23</td>\r\n  <td>A</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">CA</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">42</td>\r\n  <td>A</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">CA</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">4</td>\r\n  <td>A</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">CA</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2</td>\r\n  <td>B</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">CA</td>\r\n  <td align=\"ri