     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div>Read the next argument to `facet_grid`, `spaces`. Also, be sure to include the group when you respond to emails. </div><div><br></div><br><div><div>On Mar 5, 2014, at 7:25 AM, J H &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">renalcl...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Doug, Thanks.  However one other question.  While this does the trick it makes the box plot much larger in comparison to the other boxplots.  Is there a way to force the width of the boxplot to be the same?  Thanks. J<br>\r\n</div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Mar 4, 2014 at 8:40 PM, Doug Mitarotonda <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dougmit...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">See ?facet_grid. There is a `scales` argument. You want &quot;free_x&quot; in this case.<div>\r\n\r\n<br><div><div><div><div>On Mar 4, 2014, at 8:24 PM, J H &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">renalcl...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></div></div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">Here is the plot<br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Mar 4, 2014 at 8:23 PM, J H <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">renalcl...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I am using facet to plot box plots.  the facets are separated by 2 states, however, one of the x axis categories does not apply for one of the states. Since there is no data for that category.  I do not want to show it at all in the plot.  Is there a way to limit that?  here is the code and data.  Basically I don&#39;t want category &quot;B&quot; to be show for state NY.<br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<br>Thanks,<br><br><br><br></div><u><b>CODE</b></u><br>ggplot(table, aes(x=Category, y=Value, fill=Category)) + geom_boxplot()+ facet_grid(.~ State)<br><div><br><br><u><b>DATA</b></u><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:195pt\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"195\">\r\n\r\n <colgroup><col style=\"width:65pt\" span=\"3\" width=\"65\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt;width:65pt\" height=\"15\" width=\"65\">State</td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:65pt\" width=\"65\">Value</td>\r\n  <td style=\"width:65pt\" width=\"65\">Category</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">CA</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">323</td>\r\n  <td>A</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">CA</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">23</td>\r\n  <td>A</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">CA</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">42</td>\r\n  <td>A</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">CA</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">4</td>\r\n  <td>A</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">CA</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2</td>\r\n  <td>B</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">CA</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">42</td>\r\n  <td>B</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">CA</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">342</td>\r\n  <td>B</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">CA</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">4</td>\r\n  <td>B</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">CA</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">23</td>\r\n  <td>C</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">CA</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">42</td>\r\n  <td>C</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">CA</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">2</td>\r\n  <td>C</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr style=\"height:15pt\" height=\"15\">\r\n  <td style=\"heig